<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudra Pratap Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1531</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudra Pratap Singh was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> chief who founded Orchha in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> in 1531, on an island in the Betwa river, and made it his capital. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelas">Bundelas</a> had risen in the region after the decline of earlier powers. He died the same year, and his successors built the palaces and temples of Orchha and later allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>.</p></div>
